# Wave 0 Log

## Status

- Started: 2026-09-21
- Scope: Next.js App Router, basic Client UI, health Route Handler, SQLite connection, test runner
- Status: Complete with follow-up items

## Confirmed Decisions

- The application will be implemented under the project-root `app/` directory.
- Client UI and Backend API will be provided by one Next.js application.
- Backend endpoints will use Next.js Route Handlers under `app/api/**/route.ts`.
- Server-only modules will be placed under `app/lib/server/`.
- SQLite will use Node's built-in `node:sqlite` API.
- The project targets Node.js 22 or newer.

## Findings

### W0-001: Repository had no Next.js application scaffold

- Observation: There was no `package.json`, `app/`, `tsconfig.json`, or Next.js configuration.
- Action: Created the initial Next.js TypeScript scaffold, App Router page, health Route Handler, SQLite module, and test file.
- Follow-up: Install dependencies and run the Wave 0 verification commands.

### W0-002: Node runtime supports `node:sqlite`

- Observation: The available runtime is Node v26.7.0 and `node:sqlite` loads successfully.
- Decision: Use `node:sqlite` instead of adding a native SQLite npm dependency for the initial local version.

## Issues / Decisions Needed

- Verify that the selected Next.js version and `serverExternalPackages` configuration work with the installed runtime.
- Decide whether the final application will keep TypeScript strict mode without exceptions.
- Confirm the production database location before packaging the desktop version.

